module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.an_omitted_optional_or_defaulted_field_typechecks_but_no_value_is_constructed

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, WholeDeclaration }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { BelowCeiling, FoundOnRung, RecurringFailureMode, RungRead }
import gunbc.guarantee_rung { Mitigatable, StructurallyGuaranteed }
import gunbc.rung_climb { ClimbableButUnbuilt }

data an_omitted_optional_or_defaulted_field_typechecks_but_no_value_is_constructed: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "an_omitted_optional_or_defaulted_field_typechecks_but_no_value_is_constructed" as NonEmptyStr,

  // STATED BY THIS ROW: found on rung 1 -- the omission is loud (a typed no-such-field runtime error),
  // but only at the first READ of the field, and nothing on the required path evaluates a witness, so
  // the error surfaces wherever the first consumer happens to run. The ceiling is the v1 literal
  // completeness check this row names, which already refuses every other omitted field.
  rung: RungRead {
    found_at: FoundOnRung { rung: Mitigatable },
    standing: BelowCeiling {
      current: FoundOnRung { rung: Mitigatable },
      ceiling: StructurallyGuaranteed,
      blocker: ClimbableButUnbuilt,
      trigger_capability: "the record-literal completeness check refusing, with a located MissingField, a literal that omits a declared field the evaluator does not construct -- an Optional field with no declared default, and a field whose declared default no evaluation route realizes -- so an Accepted literal always carries every field a read can name",
    },
  },

  receipts: [
    "INVALID STATE: a record literal omits a declared field that is Optional (`T?`) or carries a declared default (`= expr`), the literal is ACCEPTED by the v1 typecheck, and the value the interpreter builds has NO such field: the first read of it fails at runtime with `no-such-field`. The checker admits an implicit absence (or an implicit default) that no evaluation route constructs, so the accepted program and the executed value disagree on the record's field set.",
    "WHY THE CHECKER ADMITS IT: v1.compiler.infer declared_field_is_required answers `return_cardinality != CardOptional && body == none`, so infer_record_lit_structural owes a MissingField only for a non-optional field with no default. Both exemptions presume the omitted field is filled in at construction; the interpreter fills neither. The exemption for Optional is also an implicit absence injection, which ruling `gunbc.design_ruling explicit_present_is_the_authoring_policy` does not admit until a declared coercion route exists.",
    "SPECIMEN (2026-10-29, found by proud-bat-605, repaired by cool-owl-599): #15347 added `redfish_accounts: List<BmcRedfishAccount>? = none` to gunbc.bmc_model BmcWorld. Three raw literals in test.claim.machine_intake.machine_intake_prior_life_boundary_witness and test.claim.machine_intake.mtcollins1_boot_acceptance_matrix omitted it and still typechecked; gunbc.bmc_model bmc_with_record_surfaces reads `world.redfish_accounts`, so on main 615d2defd058 nine of the ten prior_life_boundary claims FAIL with `runtime error [no-such-field]: no field 'redfish_accounts' on type 'BmcWorld'` (claim_batch --wet, full file). With the three literals naming the field explicitly, the same file is 10/10.",
    "THE PROBE THAT MISSED IT, kept as the reusable lesson: #15347 shipped bmc_world_literal_omit_probe, which constructed an omitting literal and asserted a DIFFERENT field (power). It was green because construction never fails; only a read of the omitted field does. A compatibility probe for a new field must read that field from the omitting literal, or it is a decoration (DESIGN section 4b, an unauthorable RED). Deleted with the repair.",
    "MEASURED WITH THE DEFAULT REMOVED: the same omitting literal with `= none` deleted from the declaration is STILL accepted (claim_batch, zero diagnostics), because the field stays Optional. So deleting a default is not a fence; the repair at the specimen is explicit naming at every literal, which is rung 1 discipline. The v2 native route was not measured.",
    "CLIMB: refusing an omitted Optional field will refuse every existing literal that relies on the exemption. No census before climbing is required (the census prerequisite is retired by the 2026-10-30 process ruling `gunbc.design_ruling bad_process_is_worse_than_no_process`; this does not establish corpus-wide coverage); that refusal set is the wall's own, and it is why the climb is a floor change landed alone rather than inside the BMC lane that found it.",
  ],

  evidence: [
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1.compiler.infer", decl_name: "declared_field_is_required", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "gunbc.bmc_model", decl_name: "bmc_with_record_surfaces", field: WholeDeclaration },
  ],
}
